[center][size=6][b]ERVR: native VR for ELDEN RING[/b][/size]
[size=3]Your head is the camera, the weapons are in your hands, and your swing is the attack.[/size]

[b]Version 0.7.0. From the maker of [url=https://github.com/IlyaMez/SpidyVR]Spidy[/url], the Spider-Man Remastered VR mod.[/b]

[url=https://discord.gg/x27ZXDpdNt][b]Join the Discord[/b][/url]: release news first, help in #ervr-help, clips. One server for ERVR and Spidy.[/center]

[quote][size=4][b]OFFLINE OR SEAMLESS CO-OP ONLY[/b][/size]
ERVR writes the game's memory, so it runs with Easy Anti-Cheat off; the included launcher starts the game that way. [b]Never use it with EAC on or in FromSoftware's online play[/b]: that risks a ban on your account. Seamless Co-op is the multiplayer that works.[/quote]

[size=5][b]What you get[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Full stereo at your headset's resolution.[/b] An image for each eye from that eye's own camera, both at the same instant. Menus, loading screens and cutscenes go on a big screen in the headset.
[*][b]First person, in the body.[/b] Your head is the camera: look around, lean, duck. Look down and your character is there, the arms following your controllers. Strike a T-pose once and its arms take the length of yours.
[*][b]Your swing is the attack.[/b] ERVR fires the game's own attack along the blade in your hand: damage, poise, status and stamina come from the game, and a faster swing hits harder. Weapons have weight.
[*][b]A shield that blocks.[/b] Raise it in front of you to block; move it into a blow to deflect it.
[*][b]Two-hand by grabbing the hilt.[/b] Squeeze your free hand on the hilt and the game two-hands the weapon. The right trigger then fires its Ash of War, the effect without the animation.
[*][b]Spells and arrows go where your hand points.[/b]
[*][b]A weapon wheel in each hand[/b], with the game's own icons.
[*][b]A belt[/b]: your four pouch shortcut items hang at your waist; grab one and press X to use it.
[*][b]The HUD on its own panel[/b] at headset resolution, where you want it.
[*][b]Torrent[/b]: the rider and the view move with the horse.
[*][b]Seamless Co-op[/b] with friends on flat screens: they need neither ERVR nor a headset.
[*][b]Body haptics[/b] on a bHaptics TactSuit, TactSleeves and TactVisor through the bHaptics Player.
[*][b]One launcher[/b] that checks the game, the headset and your PC, sets the game up for VR and starts it with one button.
[*][b]Settings in the game's own menu[/b]: System > ERVR Settings changes turning, combat, the HUD, world scale and your body calibration without leaving the headset (patch 1.17.2).
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]ELDEN RING on Steam, patch [b]1.16.2, 1.17.1 or 1.17.2[/b] (exe 2.6.2.0, 2.7.1.0 or 2.7.2.0). A new patch needs an ERVR update.
[*]A PC VR headset with an OpenXR runtime: Meta Quest over Quest Link or Air Link, Virtual Desktop, or SteamVR (Index, Vive, Pico, Steam Link and others). Played by the author on Quest 3 and Quest Pro.
[*]A GPU that can render ELDEN RING about twice per frame, one render for each eye. The big screen view is the cheap fallback.
[*]No other mod. ERVR bundles ReShade's add-on build and does not use R.E.A.L. VR.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the zip and unpack it to a folder you can write to, such as Documents\ERVR.
[*]Start [b]ERVR Launcher.exe[/b]. If Windows says it protected your PC, choose More info, then Run anyway.
[*]Fix anything the Play tab marks: the game and its patch, the VR runtime, the headset.
[*]Connect your headset and press [b]START VR[/b]. The launcher installs ERVR into the game folder, parks flat render mods and R.E.A.L. VR leftovers (renamed, never deleted), turns off depth of field, motion blur and ray tracing, and starts the game with EAC off (through Seamless Co-op when it is installed).
[/list]

Prefer it by hand? Unpack the zip straight into ELDEN RING\Game, next to eldenring.exe, and start the game offline with EAC off yourself.

[b]Updating:[/b] unpack the new zip over the old folder and press START VR; the launcher keeps your ERVR.ini.
[b]Uninstalling:[/b] the launcher's About tab has Remove ERVR, and Play flat to switch back to the flat game.

[size=5][b]Default controls (Quest Touch)[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Your head: look, lean, duck. Left stick: walk where you look. Right stick: turn, smooth or in snaps.
[*]B: dodge, hold to sprint. A: jump (confirm in menus). Left stick click: crouch; held and tilted: the quick-slot D-pad. Right stick click: lock on.
[*]Swing a weapon to attack; the left hand attacks with the left weapon. Left trigger: guard. Left grip: skill.
[*]Free hand on the hilt and a fresh squeeze of its grip: two-hand. Right trigger while two-handing: Ash of War.
[*]A grip held with the hand still: the weapon wheel. Let go over a weapon to switch.
[*]A staff, seal or bow in a hand: its trigger casts, and the spell or arrow flies where the hand points.
[*]X: use item. Y: interact. Menu button: tap for the menu, hold for the map. In a menu the left stick moves the cursor.
[*]Valve Index: the left trackpad is the menu button, the right trackpad's edges are the D-pad, and a grip counts when squeezed.
[/list]

Every button is a key in ERVR.ini, and the launcher's Options tab has the settings players change most. The [url=https://github.com/IlyaMez/EldenringVR/blob/main/docs/PLAYERS.md]players' guide[/url] has every control, setting and fix.

[size=5][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Full stereo roughly doubles the game's render work. Lower Resolution in the launcher's Options and the game's graphics settings first.
[*]Physical melee plays no attack animation, so enemy cues that read the player's animation can differ, and co-op partners see you stand still while the enemy takes the hit.
[*]Some Ashes of War need one normal use to record their effect. Charged and stance follow-ups are not done yet.
[*]The belt, the Valve Index controls, the weapon wheel and body haptics are new and have had little headset time. Report what you see.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Help, bugs and news[/b][/size]
Ask in [b]#ervr-help[/b] on the [url=https://discord.gg/x27ZXDpdNt]Discord[/url], with Game\ERVR\ERVR.log attached (set LogLevel=debug in the launcher's Options first). Reproducible bugs can also go to the [url=https://github.com/IlyaMez/EldenringVR/issues]GitHub issue tracker[/url]. Every release is announced in #ervr-updates.

[size=5][b]Antivirus warnings and verifying the download[/b][/size]
ERVR.dll injects into a running game, and dxgi.dll is ReShade's add-on build, which is unsigned by design. Generic antivirus detections are therefore possible. Every release is built from the public tagged source by GitHub Actions and carries a signed provenance attestation and a SHA256 file; this Nexus file is the same zip as the GitHub release.

[code]gh attestation verify ERVR-v0.7.0.zip --repo IlyaMez/EldenringVR[/code]

[b]ERVR has no telemetry, analytics, auto-updater or network code of its own.[/b] For body haptics it loads bHaptics' own library, which talks to the bHaptics Player on your PC; [b][bHaptics] Level=0[/b] keeps it from loading.

[size=5][b]Support ERVR[/b][/size]
ERVR is free: every release, the whole mod. A tip on [url=https://ko-fi.com/ilyamezerowsky]Ko-fi[/url] pays for updates and for the next full VR conversion; it unlocks nothing.

